+### Compound Format
+
+Pass `compound: true` to combine units, largest first. The output is compatible with Go's `time.ParseDuration`: no spaces, and hours are the largest unit (never days). Zero parts are skipped and leftover milliseconds are dropped. It only applies to the short format and is ignored when `long` is `true`.
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })       // "1h30m"
+ms(90060000, { compound: true })      // "25h1m"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })      // "-1h30m"
+ms(500, { compound: true })           // "0s"
+```
+
